259
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:06,470
Hey.

260
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:08,940
What is it?

261
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,906
Lucy's your friend, isn't he?

262
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,220
Kobe, you like Luffy Land?

263
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,797
Nuh—uh, he's a foe.

264
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:16,400
Yeah, right.

265
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:17,510
Don't

266
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:19,037
worry, we won't tell.

267
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,697
I think we should have a little talk.

268
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:23,697
I'm a Navy officer, and
I need to get going.

269
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:24,610
But

270
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:27,277
you looked so happy when
you were reading the paper.

271
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,190
paper

272
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:30,197
That's because I, uh...

273
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,110
Come on, let's talk.

274
00:14:31,193 --> 00:14:32,357
No, please stop.

275
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:35,500
Oh, Luffy Lund's in this article, too.

276
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,720
Yes, so you are his friend.

277
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:50,717
Damn my bounty only increased because of

278
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:54,660
Jerema's bad rep that takes
all the fun out of it.

279
00:14:58,400 --> 00:15:00,260
Hey, are you okay?

280
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:11,380
Just look, my bounty's gone down.

281
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:16,060
You see, it's 150 million.

282
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,760
Are you sure?

283
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,720
Wasn't it 500 a while back?

284
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,757
That went down by a whole lot.

285
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:27,077
It's even lower than it was two years ago.

286
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,395
How is that possible?

287
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,178
Did you do something wrong, perhaps?

288
00:15:31,980 --> 00:15:33,257
Isn't that backwards?

289
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:35,620
Oh, yes, you're right.

290
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:38,640
No biggie.

291
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:41,177
Less people will be after your head now.

292
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:43,000
Nami, how could you say that?

293
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:44,460
Luffy is our captain.

294
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:46,288
It could harm our prestige.

295
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,660
Damn it! Why?!

296
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:53,440
Ready the cannons!

297
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:54,920
And fire!

298
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:00,880
Let's go!

299
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,500
Have anything left by down!

300
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:07,680
What the hell is the Navy doing?

301
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:10,174
I thought they were here to protect us.

302
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,639
You'll pay for destroying our ship.

303
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:16,760
Take him out!

304
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,610
Momohahaha!

305
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:26,080
The Navy's just a joke.

306
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,797
Lucky us!

307
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:32,840
The Lucia king is away for the reverie,
and he took all his best soldiers with him.

308
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:37,960
For pirates like me, an unguarded country
like this is ripe for the picking.

309
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,760
Now listen up and listen well.

310
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:46,417
Have you ever heard of the
Emperor of the Sea, Blackbeard?

311
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:49,860
I work under him, and I've
taken the name Peachbeard.

312
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,660
You would do well to remember it.

313
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:54,980
Fear, Blackbeard!

314
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,400
All right, gentlemen,

315
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:02,819
let's start loading up the ships
and make our leader proud, shall we?

316
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:11,620
Gotcha, now empty those pockets.

317
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:13,960
Okay, just get off of me.

318
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,740
It's no use trying to get away.

319
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,941
We'll burn this whole place down.

320
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,120
Can you stand?

321
00:17:23,320 --> 00:17:24,849
Let's get you out of here.

322
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:34,186
Hey, you better not let
that girl escape, huh?

323
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,260
Not so fast.

324
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:41,761
What's that you got there, missy?

325
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,510
Now,

326
00:17:43,593 --> 00:17:48,342
what in the world could be so precious that
you would dare try and hide it from me?

327
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:49,960
Sorry, sir. Huh?

328
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,180
Is that milk?

329
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:53,537
I thought it would be money.

330
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,940
No big deal.

331
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,400
I'll take it anyway.

332
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:58,090
Please, mister.

333
00:17:58,173 --> 00:18:00,513
This is for the children of the village.

334
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:01,660
Ah, shut up!

335
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:10,336
You're really willing to
risk your life for some milk?

336
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:16,200
Please give it back to me. I beg of you.

337
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,760
It's not much, but we need it.

338
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:20,850
Huh?

339
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,900
Why don't you hand over your money, too?

340
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:25,480
I don't have any.

341
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:28,500
I bet you have your
heavenly tribute, though.

342
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,270
Yes,

343
00:18:30,353 --> 00:18:31,957
but the heavenly tribute
is what we have to

344
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,511
pay to the king and the Celestial Dragons.

345
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:36,620
We're barely getting by as is.

346
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:39,517
It takes every last berry
we can scrape together.

347
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:43,017
If we can't pay the heavenly
tribute, we'll be put to death.

348
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:44,100
What a shame.

349
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:46,060
Your king sounds terrible.

350
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:48,600
I guess I have no choice.

351
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:52,040
You fellas know what to do.

352
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:55,756
Rip this town apart and find
where they hid the money!

353
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:58,032
It's gotta be somewhere!

354
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,210
We're gonna be rich!

355
00:18:59,293 --> 00:19:00,123
No, don't!

356
00:19:00,206 --> 00:19:02,940
Tell us, where's the tribute stashed away?

357
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,460
Just leave us alone!

358
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,020
Our town has nothing!

359
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,697
Please don't take this money!

360
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:08,610
It's all I have!

361
00:19:08,693 --> 00:19:10,169
Get your grubby hands off!

362
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:12,740
Someone help!

363
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:16,737
You wouldn't have gotten beaten if
you had given us what we wanted!

364
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:18,940
Kill everyone who disobeys!

365
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,380
We've suffered enough!

366
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:25,180
Please leave our people alone! Huh?

367
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,540
Shut your trap!

368
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:32,940
Morley, let's do this. Huh?

369
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:35,660
And just who the hell are you?

370
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,120
Why is the ground shaking?

371
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:52,314
Something is coming up from the street!

372
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:01,400
What the hell?

373
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,580
Why is a huge-ass trident here?

374
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:11,130
Huh?

375
00:20:11,213 --> 00:20:12,197
Is that a giant?

376
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:17,220
One, two, one, two, one,

377
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:20,220
two, one, two, one, two!

378
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:28,160
What the hell was this
huge guy doing underground?

379
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,320
That's, uh, some outfit man.

380
00:20:32,220 --> 00:20:34,960
Uh, why is he wearing a mini skirt?

381
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,260
Don't be a creep.

382
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,228
Watch where you're looking.

383
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:44,230
Hmm.

384
00:20:44,313 --> 00:20:46,060
Hey, buddy, my eyes are up here.

385
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:49,340
If you're that into me,
then just say it, bro.

386
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:51,760
Where did you get that idea?

387
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,647
Those are some mighty
tall accusations there.

388
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,300
I've had enough of you.

389
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:57,680
Just shoot this guy.

390
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,160
You little boys should leave me alone.

391
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:08,980
So, since when do giants live underground?

392
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:10,917
I've never seen one before.

393
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,177
I wonder who this guy is.

394
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:16,240
Big ol' meanies like you will be punished!

395
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:17,610
Let's go!

396
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:21,595
How is this guy pushing the
root around like it's clay?

397
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:22,621
Don't back down!

398
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:24,172
It's only a Devil Fruit!

399
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:26,140
He's so tough.

400
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:28,940
So, what do you want to do?

401
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:33,620
Use submissive pieces of trash.

402
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,600
Hey, that's rude.

403
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,760
What do you suggest we do?

404
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:39,610
Excuse me?

405
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:42,896
Who are you people and what
do you want with our town?

406
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:53,980
Oh my!

407
00:21:55,180 --> 00:21:56,520
Now, now, Morley!

408
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:58,680
Don't have all the fun without me!

409
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:00,820
What do you want?

410
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:05,477
Wait a sec, I've got some
newly invented weapons to try!

411
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:07,560
What, you run out ahead, huh?

412
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:10,555
Who the hell are these circus monkeys?

413
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,700
Why's the murder of crows here?

414
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:22,440
Captain, look, someone's on the roof.

415
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:24,550
What?

416
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:27,400
Why are the birds gathering up?

417
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:39,740
How dare you attempt to harm the innocent?

418
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,190
Oh!

419
00:22:42,273 --> 00:22:43,380
Captain Peachbeard, sir!

420
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:45,220
They shouldn't be here!

421
00:22:45,580 --> 00:22:48,345
They're supposed to be
scared across the world!

422
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:53,120
They're the four captains
of the Revolutionary Army!

423
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,940
Wait! No, wait!

424
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:59,240
They're what?!

425
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:01,860
Knock it off!

426
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:03,420
You're still staring!

427
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:07,780
Are you scared yet, scumbag?

428
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:11,820
I'm dying to try my new weapons on you!

429
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,940
We won't allow you to do as you please.

430
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:20,301
Revolutionaries?

431
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:21,900
Are they here to help?

432
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:30,477
Heee-haw!

433
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:33,220
Strawboy really is
something else, isn't he?

434
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:36,678
I guess the apple doesn't
fall too far from the tree.

435
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:37,980
It's crazy!

436
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:42,457
Who knew that young Buck Sanji
was Jeremiah Double Six's prince?

437
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:43,660
How insolent!

438
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:45,857
He didn't even mention it to me once!

439
00:23:45,940 --> 00:23:47,400
It pisses me off.

440
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:49,717
As a result of that whole cake incident,

441
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,297
And Jarema's been booted
from the world's government.

442
00:23:52,380 --> 00:23:54,520
My, my, Straw Boy and Sanji Boy.

443
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,882
It's just as I expected, though.

444
00:23:57,400 --> 00:24:01,224
They're becoming the center of
attention in the Great Pirate Era.

445
00:24:01,740 --> 00:24:04,120
I'm excited to see where this goes.

446
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:09,317
Anyway, our officers are running
kind of late, aren't they?

447
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:12,417
Hopefully they didn't get held
up too bad on their way here.

448
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:13,330
No kidding.

449
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:18,420
By the way, Sabo, what you got
going on over there, honey pie?

450
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,060
Let me guess,

451
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:22,697
your face is cramping because you keep

452
00:24:22,780 --> 00:24:25,177
smiling every time you
think of the Luffy news,

453
00:24:25,260 --> 00:24:26,090
right?

454
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,060
You boob!

455
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:31,640
Hello, Lindbergh here!

456
00:24:31,860 --> 00:24:33,917
You guys are really
late, what's the hold-up?

457
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,180
Oh, hey, Sabo!

458
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,740
We are almost there!

459
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,540
We ran into some trouble!

460
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:41,096
Do you guys mind if we're a bit late?

461
00:24:41,460 --> 00:24:43,220
No problem, just stay safe.

462
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:46,737
Oh, I am absolutely thrilled!

463
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:51,291
All of the Revolutionary Army's best
will be here in the flesh at long last!

464
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:53,617
I can't believe I'll
get to chat with Morley!

465
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:54,840
Oh, who cares?

466
00:24:54,980 --> 00:24:56,215
It's all about Betty!

467
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:59,520
Sabo, we've wasted enough time.

468
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:01,477
We should hold our meeting now.

469
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:04,736
We might as well solidify
our plan before they arrive.

470
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:06,460
Looks like you're up, Mr.

471
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:08,300
Second-in-Command. Yep.

472
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:13,061
With the reverie just around the
corner, we'll finally take action.

473
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,800
We will be declaring war.

474
00:25:17,820 --> 00:25:19,760
On the Celestial Dragons.

475
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:23,517
The Revolutionary Army.

476
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,517
They're all so powerful.

477
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:27,940
I can't believe it!

478
00:25:30,380 --> 00:25:33,960
Why are four top officers
needed to defend one town?

479
00:25:34,260 --> 00:25:36,117
Jeez, this guy is so dense.

480
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:38,957
He only wants you for
your body, obviously.

481
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:41,177
Yuck, no thank you!

482
00:25:41,260 --> 00:25:43,577
Hey, I checked with Zeff like you asked.

483
00:25:43,660 --> 00:25:45,189
Can we do this now, Betty?

484
00:25:45,620 --> 00:25:48,000
Your power list is stopless, eh?

485
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:50,600
Why is no one answering the question?

486
00:25:50,940 --> 00:25:53,520
And what is he mumbling about, anyway?

487
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:56,100
I've had enough of you.

488
00:25:56,340 --> 00:25:57,700
Did this guy just snap?

489
00:25:58,660 --> 00:26:01,420
Hey, you pieces of
crap. You're gonna help?

490
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:04,340
Will you die or will you fight?

491
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:08,560
It's time to choose your destiny!

492
00:26:11,620 --> 00:26:14,680
Is playing hero someone else's job?!

493
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:20,260
Are you just going to cower in fear?!

494
00:26:37,380 --> 00:26:38,500
I'm here!

495
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:39,950
Momo!

496
00:26:40,780 --> 00:26:44,097
Do you really think a couple
of sticks are gonna stop us?

497
00:26:44,180 --> 00:26:45,860
You guys are cracking me up!

498
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,980
What is this, a peasant uprising?

499
00:26:50,260 --> 00:26:54,497
I'm not sure why, but all of a sudden I
feel this huge surge of power inside me.

500
00:26:54,580 --> 00:26:56,817
Yeah, let's force these pirates to leave.

501
00:26:56,900 --> 00:26:59,960
We should fight and
protect our kingdom. Yeah!

502
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:03,380
That's the stuff.

503
00:27:03,660 --> 00:27:06,717
You're feeling the raw power
of Betty's pump-pump fruit.

504
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:11,212
With a mere wave of her banner, she
can call forth the strength within you.

505
00:27:11,540 --> 00:27:14,020
Betty is a flag bearer of freedom!

506
00:27:14,820 --> 00:27:16,380
Now, let's go!

507
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:25,757
Well, I guess they want to see
what bullets do to their bodies.

508
00:27:25,840 --> 00:27:27,958
They don't know what they're in for.

509
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:32,580
Hey, Lin, Karasu, go and back them up!

510
00:27:32,820 --> 00:27:33,860
As you wish!

511
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:35,350
Now freeze!

512
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:36,860
Cool shooter!

513
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:39,660
That's freezing!

514
00:27:39,980 --> 00:27:41,400
My gun got all iced up!

515
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:43,954
How dare you attack those you bastards!

516
00:27:46,780 --> 00:27:47,960
Don't back down!

517
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:49,460
Rip them to shreds!

518
00:27:50,540 --> 00:27:51,560
Disarmed at me.

519
00:27:57,260 --> 00:28:00,660
The frickin' bird's door door! Come back!

520
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:02,320
It's all up to you!

521
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:04,180
Seize your own fate!

522
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:05,680
Now go!

523
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:08,180
Run in hell!

524
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:15,590
What is this?

525
00:28:15,673 --> 00:28:17,240
Why are they fired up?

526
00:28:17,380 --> 00:28:18,637
You jerk!

527
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:21,200
This is for the milk!

528
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:24,720
I'm taking it back!

529
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:46,477
We're out of here.

530
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:48,920
We'll make you pay for this!

531
00:28:50,740 --> 00:28:53,120
Peachbeard, 52 million berries, huh?

532
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:58,240
Master Blackbeard will avenge
me, then you'll be sorry.

533
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:02,718
I hate to break it to you, but he
doesn't give a crap about his thugs.

534
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,840
Man, what's your problem?

535
00:29:05,100 --> 00:29:06,041
You're annoying.

536
00:29:06,980 --> 00:29:07,810
Agreed.

537
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:12,620
Listen up, you pathetic,
yellow-bellied, weak, sad sacks.

538
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:17,517
All you gotta do is give
them to the world government.

539
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:19,920
And that sweet bounty will be yours.

540
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:23,757
That would be a total
of 52 million berries.

541
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:26,780
So, make sure to use it wisely.

542
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:32,200
Here, I want you to have this.

543
00:29:33,140 --> 00:29:36,120
You can use it to contact
the Revolutionary Army.

544
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:41,940
You all made me proud today.

545
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:48,380
Just hit us up anytime when the
week stand up for themselves.

546
00:29:48,860 --> 00:29:51,800
We will always be close
behind and ready to fight

547
00:30:11,940 --> 00:30:13,837
I can't thank you enough for this!

548
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:16,038
We'll never forget what you've done!

549
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:28,598
Say, what exactly is the reason we're
meeting up with everyone anyway?

550
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,777
We'll be picking a fight
with the Celestial Dragons.

551
00:30:31,860 --> 00:30:34,760
Oh, now that sounds like
a good time! Heck yeah!

552
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:36,920
Oh, one thing, Karasu.

553
00:30:37,280 --> 00:30:39,720
You need to turn off your loudspeaker!

554
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:44,220
Sorry. Forgot.

555
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:50,357
Only two days remain until
the reverie and the schemes

556
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:53,860
of players from around the
world begin to intertwine.

557
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:57,160
Okay, roger that.

558
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:00,817
I have an update for you. Sabo?

559
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:02,440
They'll be here soon.

560
00:31:03,140 --> 00:31:03,970
Alright.

561
00:31:05,520 --> 00:31:06,880
Let's do this.

562
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:12,137
What is this crap?

563
00:31:12,220 --> 00:31:14,897
I've seen this stupid face before.

564
00:31:14,980 --> 00:31:18,737
This is the same guy who screwed
over my entire smile production.

565
00:31:18,820 --> 00:31:22,280
How in the hell did he manage
to take down that old bag?

566
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:32,157
It says he won.

567
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:34,697
What the hell?

568
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:36,257
When did I lose?

569
00:31:36,340 --> 00:31:37,397
And to whom?

570
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:40,617
I think I know who wrote
this slanderous article.

571
00:31:40,700 --> 00:31:42,937
Mama, I do too.

572
00:31:43,020 --> 00:31:45,717
I'll have to teach Morgan's a lesson,

573
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:51,180
but Straw Hat, you're first!

574
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:54,397
I'll be coming for you.

575
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:59,457
The fifth Emperor now—that

576
00:31:59,540 --> 00:32:01,597
title doesn't fit you at all!

577
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:02,510
Looks

578
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:14,820
like I'll be seeing you soon. Luffy.

579
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:18,370
Luffy

580
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,600
So what if it got lower?

581
00:32:29,840 --> 00:32:31,075
We can't do anything.

582
00:32:31,320 --> 00:32:33,037
You'll get up there again, Loopy.

583
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:34,780
You know I got your back.

584
00:32:35,060 --> 00:32:36,531
We'll get it even higher.

585
00:32:36,760 --> 00:32:37,590
You hungry?

586
00:32:37,673 --> 00:32:38,740
I'll make lunch.

587
00:32:47,280 --> 00:32:48,840
Uh, just a moment.

588
00:32:54,240 --> 00:32:59,060
Look, I believe you missed
a few zeros here, Luffy.

589
00:32:59,680 --> 00:33:00,680
Unreal.

590
00:33:03,860 --> 00:33:07,240
Your bounty's not 150 million.

591
00:33:09,460 --> 00:33:12,300
It's 1.5 billion!

592
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:22,777
While the rest of the world
looks towards the reverie,

593
00:33:22,860 --> 00:33:25,480
the Straw Hats embark to the land of Wano.
